Commit d2f99e08, parked on phase/8.4 (tag deleted 2026-10-16)
Subject: fix(write): a shared title word must distinguish its record, not just name it

Card 25 (2026-09-25). _names_its_record in synthesis/grounding.py
accepted a reworded sentence that switched to a different record on
any shared content word with that record's title, including generic
clinical vocabulary a record didn't own alone. Measured: after a
Tay-Sachs sentence, "No patient carried more than one of these
mutations" cited a BRCA paper whose title also says "patients".

Fixed structurally, no stop-word list: a shared word only counts when
it does not also appear in every OTHER cited record's title in the
same answer. run_grounding_pass now builds that other-records label
text and passes it alongside the switched-to record's own title.
Replays the Tay-Sachs/BRCA case as a unit test and proves a genuinely
distinguishing word still licenses a switch.


